6. Investment arguments

# Look at the core logic (3 pieces)

1. ** The profit-making trap has arrived and the profit-release period**: the Māori rate has improved for 15 consecutive quarters (26 to 37 per cent), with management directing Māori to 40-45 per cent in 2026 and business profit 15-20 per cent. If realized, this means that operating profits may leapfrog from about RMB 2 billion in 2025 to RMB 5-6 billion, with a high degree of profit growth.

2. ** The advertising conversion early**: The rate of loading of the advertising at Station B is much lower than that of the peers, and the advertising revenue has become the largest source of income (year-on-year + 23%). The efficiency of the advertising unit for tremors is being realized, and the advertising at Station B has several times the scope for upgrading, which is an undervalued growth engine.

3. ** The unique community moat river is ignored by the market**: Although morning stars are rated as "the moat river", the culture of the screen, the identity of young users and the high-time stickyness of station B are unique in the Chinese Internet. 366 million MAU, the average of almost two hours, attests to the continued healthy functioning of the community.

# Look out core logic (3 bars)

1. ** The reality of the unguarded river**: The morning star's "guardless river" rating is based on facts. Station B's content production is based on creators, whose distribution is multiplatform and users can move at any time. Under the siege of the shivering and fast hands, the station B's moat is essentially a "cultural identity" rather than a structural barrier.

2. ** Growth has slowed**: Q1,2026 income growth has fallen to 7%, which is continuing to slow down from 19% in 2024 and 13% in 2025. With MAU approaching 370 million, the ceiling may be close to growth for users, with future growth relying more on more liquidity efficiency than on expansion.

** Valuation may not be as cheap as it looks**: if GAAP PE (~55x) is used, station B will remain a high value. The latest morning star data suggest that fair value may have been reduced from $36, meaning that current stock prices do not necessarily mean that 83% are actually underestimated. Investors need to be cautious about the source and timeliness of valuation data.

