Conclusion

** Whether or not it is worth studying in depth: two prerequisites need to be tested, although it is worth noting.**

The story of the B-site investment is essentially a "profit release" narrative: moving from loss to profit, from inefficient to efficient. The first year of profit in 2025 is a positive sign, and the continued improvement in the Māori rate is encouraging.

The following prerequisites, however, need to be validated:
1. ** Whether the Māori and 15-20% operating profit rates, as directed by management, will be realized by 2026**. If implemented, the current valuation is indeed attractive; if not, it will severely undermine market confidence.
2. **DAU/MAU ratio and user time are sustainable**. This is the core health indicator of the community-based platform and all realization assumptions need to be reassessed in the event of a downward trend.

** Special reminder**: Morning Star gives station B a "Campless River" rating, and the latest data suggests that fair value may have been lowered. Users need to verify the timeliness of the data when using a fair value of $36. From a cautious perspective, station B is more suitable for a speculative model of "high resilience, high uncertainty" than "undervalued value investment".

